# id|label|repo|ref|description. repo is a git URL or path relative to project root starting with '/'.
# ref is a git tag or branch, or "-" for the default branch; ignored for local directories.
# Each source must have install.sh at its root. Ids must be unique across desktops.list.

# DEs
gnome|GNOME|/gnome|-|Modern, polished, Wayland-first desktop|desktop
xfce|Xfce|/xfce|-|Lightweight traditional desktop|desktop
kde|KDE Plasma|/kde|-|Highly configurable, feature-rich desktop|desktop
lxqt|LXQt|/lxqt|-|Very lightweight desktop, good for old hardware|desktop
cosmic|Cosmic|/cosmic|-|Modern Gnome-Inspired desktop (Unofficial Trixie build)|desktop
mate|MATE|/mate|-|Lightweight GNOME 2 successor|desktop
cinnamon|Cinnamon|/cinnamon|-|Traditional desktop with Windows-style layout|desktop

## WMs
openbox|Openbox|/openbox|-|Minimal stacking window manager|x11
i3|i3|/i3|-|Tiling window manager for X11|x11
labwc|labwc|/labwc|-|Wayland window manager with floating windows, inspired by Openbox|wayland
sway|Sway|/sway|-|Tiling window manager for Wayland inspired by i3|wayland
hyprland|Hyprland|/hyprland|-|Highly-customizable tiling compositor for Wayland (Backported)|wayland
